{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463875-questions-about-weapons-made-partially-of-silver-and-garou","id":1463875,"title":"Questions about weapons made ( partially ) of silver and garou","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-10-14T12:56:41-07:00","id":1463875,"title":"Questions about weapons made ( partially ) of silver and garou","content":"Silver is not SO bad for weapons. It's quite heavy and hard, it can be done. Yet it's not the best choice if your life depends on it.<br /> So, I came up with some ideas. But I don't know how much effective would they be against a garou.<br /> I would like to hear your opinions.<br /> <br /> <i><b>I'm talking about knives, machetes or shortswords, NOT bullets.</b></i><br /> <br /> 1- a blade made of steel with a thick silver plating?<br /> 2- a blade with a body of steel ( for durability ) and the edge made in silver ( for damage )?<br /> 3- a silver / steel alloy?<br /> <br /> A more specific question is: what would bite more deeply in the extremely hard skin and muscles of a garou: steel or silver? For sure silver causes more damage as soon it penetrates, but mabye steel - harder and sharper - has an easier time entering.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27051-solomon-draak","name":"Solomon Draak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27051_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-14T15:14:16-07:00","id":1463889,"title":"","content":"Skip blades if you're not using magic. You don't need to cut to hurt a Garou. Make bludgeoning weapons with a silver impact tool on the end of a strong material that isn't going to break under the weight, and probably want to avoid metal so it doesn't get too heavy to use. A two pound ball of silver on the end of a proper wooden handle is plenty dangerous to a Garou. You don't have to figure out how to hone a blade, or worry about the rules on how much you can alloy the silver before it's too impure to do Agg. Sure the mace will deform a bit with use... but you can just press it back into shape between fights.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-14T15:46:05-07:00","id":1463893,"title":"","content":"I liked the fight description in Possessed: a player's guide, where a Gorehound fomor gives to <i><b>three</b></i> garou the fight of their life out of sheer rage and resilience.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;As we were looking around trying to get a grip on the place, Lys cries out in pain and falls over with a knife sticking out of her side. The guy just popped out of nowhere, and he was carrying a fire ax completely soaked in blood. We won the fight, obviously, but if Corina hadn't come back up to check on us, I'm not sure how it would have gone. As it was, that guy took more hits before dropping than some werewolves I fought. And damn, could he dish it out! You see this scar? </div> </div> </div>So I thought: what if the gorehound, instead of using improvised implements ( although it was fully appropriate for the Gorehound gimmick to do so ) used instead a finely balanced, silver-edged personalized combat knife?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27051-solomon-draak","name":"Solomon Draak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27051_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-14T16:10:46-07:00","id":1463900,"title":"","content":"According to the rules, his first attack would be aggravated and then the rest bashing as the knife's edge gets too mangled to be effective after one hit. Which is fairly accurate to whole silver that pure would hold up to combat use.<br /> <br /> A silver knife might look cool, but without magic to make it a real combat knife, it's kinda pointless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-14T16:52:51-07:00","id":1463909,"title":"","content":"One thing to remember is that there is not any scientific reason why silver harms Garou. It's magic. It has mystical properties since it's the &quot;lunar metal&quot; and considered to be a protective agent in folklore. You don't need to worry about whether a silver blade can realistically pierce the hard, leathery skin of the Crinos form. It'll cut through it just because it is silver with a sharp edge.<br /> <br /> RPGs have always struggled on handling silver weapons. Does it need to be pure silver? Can it just be silver clad over a weapon made from steel? It's a balance of what is needed for the game, real world scarcity and cost (or lack thereof), and genre considerations (the needs of a fantasy game like D&amp;D where lycanthropes are an occasional monster is different than a gothic horror game with werewolves as the protagonist). Different people will like a different balance.<br /> <br /> For me, the entire weapon needs to be almost entirely silver. It doesn't need to be 100% pure, but close enough. Too much presence of other metals, whether in the form of composition, alloy, or underneath the clad, &quot;pollutes&quot; the mystic properties that silver has against the Garou. That limits its applications. You can't make swords with it. The silver dagger is iconic for a reason. We should go with that. That also means that similar sized weapons - arrow heads and spears - can also work. That also means such a weapon has a limited lifespan because it'll be deformed quickly during combat. So you'll need to reforge it or make a new one.<br /> <br /> That seems to work for me. But I'm open to good alternatives.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-17T11:43:38-07:00","id":1464272,"title":"","content":"Silver isn\u2019t as strong as steel, but it\u2019s not Play-Doh. It\u2019s strong enough for plenty of weapons, just not some others. Silver is a very heavy metal, only slightly less dense than lead. That makes it bad for swords. It\u2019s softness also makes it bad for swords. It would probably bend if you made it into a sword and used it significantly, plus it would be hard to wield since it\u2019s so heavy. A silver mace, though, would work just fine. A silver knife might also be more likely to bend unless it were designed to be unusually thick. Silver knuckles might be a better choice for an easily concealable silver weapon.<br /> <br /> Silver spear heads, arrow/bolt heads, axes, hammers, maces, bullets, picks, and maces should all work just fine. In the origin Wolfman movie, he killed a werewolf with a silver headed cane, that would work too. <br /> <br /> Really, the main weapon that doesn\u2019t work when it\u2019s made of silver are swords, there are so many others that work. <br /> <br /> As for purity of silver, my own ruling is that if a reasonable person would consider it silver, then the spirits do too. It doesn\u2019t have to be pure, but if enough impurities are added to significantly change the properties of the metal, then it\u2019s not silver anymore. If you have a silver and iron alloy that is strong and light enough to make an effective sword, it\u2019s likely not silver enough to do aggravated damage to a werewolf. <br /> <br /> Though I suppose that if you had some kind of material that\u2019s mostly silver, I might say that it does soakable aggravated damage to a werewolf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-17T16:45:49-07:00","id":1464286,"title":"","content":"Off the top of my head, at least one of the WtA books actually put the minimum at 90% silver in an alloy. Which covers a lot of standard silver alloys that are still &quot;silver&quot; to most people, such as sterling silver (which the vast majority of silver house wares and jewelry uses), and most coin silver that was used on a silver standard (once silver standards stopped being a thing, silver coins tended to be minted with less silver in them).<br /> <br /> This actually leaves Argentium silver as an available alloy, which is interesting because it can be hardened to a degree. Not enough for a sword, but enough for a knife that will survive a fight, and make any sort of blunt force weapon made of silver more practical. It's also fairly common now because it tarnishes much more slowly than standard sterling silver and thus requires a lot less polishing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-18T05:56:22-07:00","id":1464370,"title":"","content":"My two cents...<br /> <br /> I would say that even a coating of pure silver on the flat ( not the edge or the point ) of a knife would burn a garou's flesh. Mabye such a knife would deal a single aggravated damage and the rest, normal lethal damage.<br /> <br /> About the need for the silver to be at least 90% pure, it seems too much for me. I think any amount of silver on direct skin contact would cause at very least serious discomfort to a Garou, and atrocious pain if inside an open wound.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27051-solomon-draak","name":"Solomon Draak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27051_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-18T07:35:21-07:00","id":1464379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solomon Draak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463875-questions-about-weapons-made-partially-of-silver-and-garou?p=1464370#post1464370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">About the need for the silver to be at least 90% pure, it seems too much for me. I think any amount of silver on direct skin contact would cause at very least serious discomfort to a Garou, and atrocious pain if inside an open wound.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the point is, that it has to be elemental silver of a significant purity. Just adding some atoms of silver to some steel (which already is an alloy) shouldn't count. Neither is Silvernitrate, and actual molecule of silver and nitrate atoms silver, like it is shown in SONYs Underworld movies. Freak Legion, iirc, actually stated silvernitrate is poisonous and does damage as a poison, but not as silver.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, I would totally allow for silver damage from the silverware, if some human manages to get it out of the drawer in time. Even if there is a layer of silveroxid on the surface...<br /> But that is just my opinion. In most cased, the story situation demands what is correct, not the scientific explanation...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-18T13:12:15-07:00","id":1464410,"title":"","content":"In the W20 rules, it says &quot;In addition to turning normal attacks into unsoakable aggravated damage, silver causes other problems for the Garou. Just touching silver causes one level of aggravated damage per turn of contact, unless the werewolf is a homid or lupus who is in breed form.&quot;<br /> <br /> I believe that the damage caused by &quot;touch&quot; does not mention the word unsoakable is intentional.<br /> <br /> (Later the book says silver plated weapons deal damage as though they are silver, but that after several blows the plating is &quot;ruined&quot;. I chalk that up to be an attempt to reconcile game needs without making silver weapons too easily available. It doesn't seem to make actual sense to me.)<br /> <br /> So what I'd probably rule in the case of a normal knife claded in silver is that the touch of that silver clad does cause 1 level of (soakable) aggravated damage, but the rest of the damage is lethal. In contrast, using the classic &quot;silver dagger&quot; turns all your damage into unsoakable aggravated.<br /> <br /> At some point, I think adulterating silver would no longer cause aggravated damage at all by touching, though there would be pain or discomfort. I do think it should be somewhere between 80-90% pure silver which matches what the corebook tells us. One ST or another may have a definite preference for the higher or lower range of that, but I wouldn't complain too much. If it gets below 80% though, I'd probably begin complaining. I'd probably say as an ST that the 80% is fine to provide soakable aggarvated damage by touch, but that to turn a weapon into unsoakable aggravated damage you need at least 90%.<br /> <br /> My internal guidance here is what would I want to happen if I was seeing a movie or reading a book about a werewolf. Does what happen seem appropriate for the genre, or would I roll my eyes and get out of my seat in protest?<br /> <br /> Sometimes that may not lead to consistency. I have no problem with Larry Talbot beating Bela to death with a silver headed cane in the Wolf Man movie as Sergeant Brother mentioned. It seems like a good scene. But do I really want some vampire with lots of Potence and burning blood to boost his Strength to kill a werewolf with silver knuckles in one punch because his Str+1 weapon is now unsoakable aggravated? I mention that because I know there are players out there that would totally do that, and then word were spread throughout the vampire community and somehow having silver knuckles on you as a means of last resort is going to be the new status symbol, and I think that'd be awful. But how is that different than simply using a cane other than a a top heavy artistic silver headed cane is something ordinary people might want while possessing silver knuckles is something only a character in an RPG would have? I think it when comes to cases like this, I'd likely seek consensus among the players and atrribute any inconsistencies to the mercurial nature of Luna.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-19T03:15:34-07:00","id":1464491,"title":"","content":"I think that a silver plating, if more thick than normal (two or three times) and, more importantly, put only on the flat and not on the edge, should do some damage without getting ruined.<br /> The plating is not subject to impact and when the blade enters, it's silver against open flesh.<br /> <br /> Also, I think a very good weapon would be a blade with the body and the point of steel, but the lateral edges of silver. The brunt of the impact is taken by the point ( while stabbing ), while the flesh just slide on the silver edges. Of course such a weapon is suited for stabbing rather than slashing... but honestly, slashing is never a good idea.<br /> Stabs are more difficult to avoid, more precise and way more damaging.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But do I really want some vampire with lots of Potence and burning blood to boost his Strength to kill a werewolf with silver knuckles in one punch because his Str+1 weapon is now unsoakable aggravated? </div> </div> </div>In the NWod there is a vampire hunter ( in the module Antagonists ) who kills vampires with a gasoline-filled water pistol...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27051,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27051-solomon-draak","user":"Solomon Draak","date":". 10-19-2021, 06:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27051-solomon-draak","name":"Solomon Draak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27051_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-19T04:25:28-07:00","id":1464500,"title":"","content":"Plating with thicker coats doesn't inherently increase durability, after a certain point it actually can reduce it because instead of dealing with a thin layer that starts to chip or wear away from abrasion, you get a layer thick enough it can just peel off as the bond between the silver and steel gives way under the force of the weight of the silver.<br /> <br /> Which, again, brings us back to however cool silver blades are, silver bludgeoning weapons are far more practical.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-19T04:48:28-07:00","id":1464503,"title":"","content":"Your absolute best melee option is a warhammer, a warpick, or, in the interest of keeping the garou as far away as possible while still considering yourself to be in melee, a polearm. Why? All of these options allow for a dangerous and economical impact point; you only need a small surface area of silver while you never get into the finicky area of silver blades. A spike or small hammerhead are ideal, and if you've got the resources there's no problem silvering the haft. <br /> <br /> It's worth noting that Klaives and more rediculously, grand klaives are all-silver blades. The production process is magical and imbues the weapon with the weapon with some of the properties that make steel ideal for blades. If you have a magical manufacturing method, quantity becomes your only obstacle, since it's pretty hard to mass produce with magical methods. <br /> <br /> Annoyingly, while the game state that the silver needs to be very pure, it does also provide Pentex with silver nitrate bullets... maybe there's some other magic stuff in there that makes it work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-19T12:55:47-07:00","id":1464530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463875-questions-about-weapons-made-partially-of-silver-and-garou?p=1464503#post1464503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your absolute best melee option is a warhammer, a warpick, or, in the interest of keeping the garou as far away as possible while still considering yourself to be in melee, a polearm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Anyone who seriously wants to hunt lupines should not consider close melee to be the best method. A silver dagger is fine for last desperate chance at self-defense, but even supernatural opponents shouldn't want silver melee weapons that puts them in close quarters combat.<br /> <br /> I've done some thinking on this because I've wanted human hunters to be just as dangerous to werewolves as they are to vampires, but the game does not give you much support. Usually it's a supernatural based faction that has benefits as a result of supernatural backing. I wanted something that could conceivably do so without reference to other factions (True Faith is fine as religion is available to everyone, as well as anything already established in folklore, but I don't want people casting spells or using fetishes). In the original Werewolf: the Dark Ages book, but not the subsequent Dark Ages line, it mentions the Teutonic Knights as a possible mortal threat to the Garou, so I've taken that as inspiration.<br /> <br /> In so far that you want a melee weapon, it'd probably be something like a boar or bear spear. A long shaft that keeps the animal away from combined with a large spearhead and some kind of crosspiece that prevents the animal from sliding its body up the shaft. A few knights using them to keep the werewolf in place, or some kind of immobilizing trap, and then you use range weapons (like silver arrow heads) to finish the thing off. Later on in time, you just switch to silver bullets and guns and do your best to stay away. And have as many people as possible in the area so that multiple shots can go off.<br /> <br /> Now carrying around a silver headed bear spear isn't practical in the modern age, but the Teutonic Knights, various royal wolfcatchers, Society of St Leopold, and other obvious bases for medieval era werewolf hunters would probably do so. There'd even be enough of them having survived, such weapons would likely be a historical curiosity. And academic writers would do their best to explain that of course these would never have been used in actual &quot;werewolf hunting&quot;, but ornamental replicas used as a sign of status or reward. The kind of Masquerade nonsense that must be omnipresent in the World of Darkness but feeds into conspiracy and unknown mysteries fanatics (like In Search Of episodes narrated by Leonard Nimoy about werewolf hunting and filming the museum exhibits of the silver headed weapons of the Teutonic Order with a talking head on how these would have only been created if the Knights were actually engaged in hunting werewolves).<br /> <br /> For modern hunting, any silver melee weapons would need to be easily concealable. You can't go around carrying a silver headed mace. You'd either be arrested, harassed by questions, or robbed. It'd have to be something easily hidden in a pants or jacket pocket, or disguised as something else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-19T19:28:26-07:00","id":1464552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463875-questions-about-weapons-made-partially-of-silver-and-garou?p=1464503#post1464503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your absolute best melee option is a warhammer, a warpick, or, in the interest of keeping the garou as far away as possible while still considering yourself to be in melee, a polearm. Why? All of these options allow for a dangerous and economical impact point; you only need a small surface area of silver while you never get into the finicky area of silver blades. A spike or small hammerhead are ideal, and if you've got the resources there's no problem silvering the haft.<br /> <br /> It's worth noting that Klaives and more rediculously, grand klaives are all-silver blades. The production process is magical and imbues the weapon with the weapon with some of the properties that make steel ideal for blades. If you have a magical manufacturing method, quantity becomes your only obstacle, since it's pretty hard to mass produce with magical methods.<br /> <br /> Annoyingly, while the game state that the silver needs to be very pure, it does also provide Pentex with silver nitrate bullets... maybe there's some other magic stuff in there that makes it work.</div> </div> </div> </div>Silver nitrate hollow points were scrubbed in Revised. I don't know what possessed someone to make them return for W20 in the Book of the Wyrm, but they're not a welcome sight, and I can't be the only person who ignores the existence of &quot;poison rounds&quot; due to the effects of silver not working anything like what the description thinks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-19T22:39:34-07:00","id":1464562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463875-questions-about-weapons-made-partially-of-silver-and-garou?p=1464530#post1464530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Anyone who seriously wants to hunt lupines should not consider close melee to be the best method.</div> </div> </div> </div>If a Crinos was charging me down and a gun was too much trouble, I'd want nothing more than the longest pike coated in pure silver between us, but that's not the only circumstance you're going to be fighting werewolves in. <br /> <br /> 1- A small weapon is obviously much better for a sneak/suprise assassinations. Put the hammer under your, approach the homid werewolf, relentlessly slam till he's paste. If you managed to get a good angle before the attack, perhaps a stun from behind, then he won't immediately be able to kill you when he rages into crinos or escape when he fear frenzies away as a lupus. <br /> <br /> 2- You're not going to carry a spear everywhere you go. A fancy folding spear is going to waste time setting up. If you get ambushed, as a successful werewolf hunter is likely to be. You're going to need something fast. <br /> <br /> 3- Polearms are prone to getting lost. A backup is great. <br /> <br /> 4- one handed weapons have a lot of inherent advantages over two handed weapons. Like you can use a whole other hand. Considering your massive enemy, I'd very much worry about getting an arm injury and not being able to use a polearm properly. <br /> <br /> 5- If you're a supernatural hunter, you want more reach than the enemy, but you might not necessarily need polearm level reach. You can play pig to eat the tiger, or you might just want to be able to walk around without a massive amount of attention that a spear would bring you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-20T07:21:48-07:00","id":1464586,"title":"","content":"I imagine that if you saw someone walking down the street with a lucerne hammer, that the weapon itself would be rather more conspicuous than the fact that the head was silver. If we are talking about medieval or renaissance werewolf hunters, then it might be more appropriate, but even back then normal people generally needed an excuse to carry around a weapon of war.<br /> <br /> Almost any creature that wants to kill werewolves is probably going to want to avoid close combat, so even a polearm is going to be sub-optimal compared to guns. In fact, I'll say that if you are going to carry a large weapon that is hard to conceal, that a rifle or shotgun would be better than a mace or polearm. Along the same lines, for something easily concealable, a pistol with silver bullets is going to be better than a silver knife or silver knuckles. In the USA, it's actually easier to legally carry a gun than it is many sorts of far less lethal close combat weapons. As has been mentioned many other times, some kind of silver headed walking stick might be good if you're going for melee, because you don't have to conceal it, it is what it is and most people wouldn't see it is a threat and the head can be pure silver.<br /> <br /> Maybe those guys who get stopped by police with assault rifles and who say that they are exercising their right to open carry or who are sovereign citizens are just werewolf hunters.<br /> <br /> I don't worry about other creatures having too easy a time against werewolves because of silver weapon. Werewolves are unstoppable juggernauts otherwise, so I have no problem letting enemies in the know exploit their only weakness. I guess it does get a bit silly if every vampire or fomor has a silver knife or knuckles, even though it would be reasonable if they expected to fight werewolves. That kind of balancing act can be a rule, it has to be up to individual storytellers.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-20T09:07:01-07:00","id":1464593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Anyone who seriously wants to hunt lupines should not consider close melee to be the best method. </div> </div> </div>Not even a Gorehound fomor on steroids?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27051-solomon-draak","name":"Solomon Draak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27051_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-20T13:54:27-07:00","id":1464636,"title":"","content":"Even Jason Voorhees has used ranged weapons to get his kills, so it's not actually outside the Gorehound mold for that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-22T13:40:55-07:00","id":1464906,"title":"","content":"AFAIK even silver bullets are crappy and hard to make. The description of the plating being ruined is kinda silly, but what matters is the underlying reason:<br /> <br /> Silver weapons aren't reliable. They're not supposed to be. This is the core of the weakness, you have to fight a werewolf with something that isn't a weapon. Not a proper one, anyway. You improvise with spoons made of holy metal and get to cause unsoakable agg.<br /> <br /> Wanna get around it? Work hard. Casting silver into bullets takes far more skill than using lead, silver knifes need a lot more care, for every weapon there are downsides. It isn't a good weapon metal, it is a good ceremonial metal.<br /> <br /> Or just live with the inconveniences of having to weaponize personal objects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-22T14:22:09-07:00","id":1464911,"title":"","content":"How good silver bullets are is kinda variable and hard to ever really prove because nobody has yet to decide to make the massive financial investment and direct personal risk of actually using silver bullets in a true combat situation.<br /> <br /> The physics of it are the silver bullets should perform OK, but not as well as conventional bullets against humans, or at significant range. Silver is less dense than lead, which means less kinetic energy (aka damage), which is a problem there.<br /> <br /> However there's a mixed bag regarding silver's relative hardness to lead. Silver is harder. This means silver doesn't take to rifling as well as lead (decreasing its effective accuracy at range), but lots of guns still use smooth bore barrels (like shotguns) where there wouldn't be a noticeable diffeence. For the same reasons, silver doesn't deform as much on impact, leading to &quot;over-penetration&quot; in human analog targets (that is, the bullet goes through the target, imparting less force, and thus causes less tissue damage). However... over-penetration assumes normal clothing and skin. Body armor or thick hides that minimize the damage of normal bullets tend to fail against harder bullets (that's how traditional armor piercing bullets are made).<br /> <br /> Casting silver isn't actually hard, it just takes different equipment. Trying to cast silver bullets with standard bullet molds and crucibles is likely to fail horribly; hence it's seen as difficult. The problem is that silver is cast at a much higher temperature than lead, and can't be air cooled without serious risk of flaws in the final product. Proper molds that can handle the heat and not weld to the silver can be made (nobody makes them for bullets though). Cooling ovens that slowly bring the silver casting down to room temperature without flaws are things that can be acquired fairly easily even if you'll need to do some research/experimentation to get the process down (again, non-bullet stuff is out there as guides).<br /> <br /> ----------------<br /> <br /> So, gun stuff aside (though I'd hope the casting part is relevant to non-gun ideas):<br /> <br /> Yeah, silver isn't really a great weapon metal. If it was, the game probably wouldn't make it as effective against the Garou so the PCs wouldn't get slaughtered by it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-22T16:23:04-07:00","id":1464934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solomon Draak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463875-questions-about-weapons-made-partially-of-silver-and-garou?p=1464593#post1464593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not even a Gorehound fomor on steroids?</div> </div> </div> </div>Only morons would want to fight a Garou in melee combat. The best choice, if available, is always to fight them with range weapons, preferably at a long enough distance that takes more than a turn for a Garou to cover the distance. The farther, the better.<br /> <br /> It is perfectly fine if you want Gorehounds to be morons though. There's never a shortage of morons in the world. Many Fomori are in the position of morons.<br /> <br /> Regardless of the wisdom of wanting to fight Garou in melee, of course it would be better to have a silver weapon instead of a normal one. That's obvious.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463875-questions-about-weapons-made-partially-of-silver-and-garou?p=1464906#post1464906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Silver weapons aren't reliable. They're not supposed to be. This is the core of the weakness, you have to fight a werewolf with something that isn't a weapon. Not a proper one, anyway. You improvise with spoons made of holy metal and get to cause unsoakable agg.</div> </div> </div> </div>That should be true of the vast number of people in the World of Darkness. I'm not sure how one would simulate the difficulty of using improvised weapons in combat. Maybe an increase in difficulty by +1 or +2.<br /> <br /> However, I think there would be significant exceptions to the idea that silver weapons would always be improvised. The real world has no need of properly manufactured silver weapons. But there are certainly factions in Werewolf: the Apocalypse that would have need for them. PENTEX should have a proper foundry and arsenal for creating any practical silver weapons for use by its First Teams and as self defense for its personnel. They would certainly be using them to the extent that a proper foundry, mold, and other tools to mass produce silver bullets and knives to fit their needs. They certainly have the money to do so. To a much lesser degree, hunter groups like DNA or the Society of St Leopold should also have a dedicated facility to manually produce such weapons in large batches, but not to the point of mass manufacturing. Other well organized enemies of the Garou that would have the incentive, means, and organization to do something similar might include the vampire clans Tremere and Ventrue. And the Bratovitch revenants probably have an strong, independent crafts tradition of making silver weapons on their family estates. There's probably other factions I'm not thinking of that would have some kind of professional crafts tradition of making these kinds of weapons.<br /> <br /> And to be honest, there are probably enough &quot;strange requests&quot; in the WoD by more ordinary people (or seemingly so) for these kinds of weapons, that I would not be surprised if there is some kind of trade by some sort of local specialist in many places around the world. Enough gun shops, jewelers, blade smiths, and other businesses probably got enough odd requests, that eventually someone in a region includes this as part of his business even if it is only a part of what he does and never advertises it. &quot;Only for trusted clients&quot; kind of thing. And some of these other businesses begin to refer people who ask for such weapons to this guy (in whatever manner the craftsman would want, he may not his name out, but he might ask for people's names and contact info passed onto him to investigate and decide if he wants to help). He would charge a healthy premium to make these kind of silver weapons, and they would not be rush jobs, but they'd probably be of decent quality. The problem would be for an ordinary person to locate such a guy and afford his services. Such an underground trade would be perfectly fitting the gothic setting of the WoD.<br /> <br /> Not knowing much about the actual crafting of such items, I performed a quick internet search and came across this link. I have never read these books so I can't comment on that, but someone seemed to do some real research on crafting silver bullets.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.patriciabriggs.com/articles/silver/silverbullets.shtml\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.patriciabriggs.com/images/template/header.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.patriciabriggs.com/articles/silver/silverbullets.shtml\" target=\"_blank\"> Casting Silver Bullets </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.patriciabriggs.com/articles/silver/silverbullets.shtml\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.patriciabriggs.com/articles/silver/silverbullets.shtml </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Author Patricia Briggs investigates casting silver bullets. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I know silver bullets are not what the OP wanted to talk about, but some of the difficulties would apply to any kind of silver weapon.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-22T22:00:36-07:00","id":1464968,"title":"","content":"Just to clarify, when I said silver weapons aren't reliable, I'd meant it in a broad sense.<br /> <br /> You either can't rely on their quality, durability, damage rating, or things like availability and ease to get one.<br /> <br /> Groups like Pentex and St Leopold will surely have facilities just for this task. But at this point those are, trope wise, magical weapons. And what could those facilities make if they didn't had to work silver?<br /> <br /> If you try to make any weapon out of silver through regular methods, you'll have a crappy result for one reason or another. If you go through all the process to get a proper silver version, at this point it will be special just due to how hard it was to get, in time, effort and cost. And just for the benefit of being silver, maybe still with some flaws.<br /> <br /> One way or another, using a silver weapon is never a light decision.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-23T10:04:53-07:00","id":1465017,"title":"","content":"Gorehounds are regenerating berserker who love to rip their opponents to pieces. I feel they're kinda wasted by using ONLY a firearm. Mabye from distance, for softening the target a bit, but sooner or later they will charge in melee.<br /> <br /> By the description on the book, that Gorehound almost killed two Garou alone, before the third arrived. With the advantage of a surprise attack on the first, ok.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27051-solomon-draak","name":"Solomon Draak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27051_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-23T16:34:55-07:00","id":1465061,"title":"","content":"And doesn't need a silver weapon to do so. I once surprised an ST by taking down a BSD with bashing damage in a grapple (the scene was in public, so shifting or using weapons would have caused other problems) as they weren't expecting the PCs to call the BSD's bluff around a fight in the situation. Damage, in the end, is damage. Silver takes Garou out faster, but any damage will eventually win.<br /> <br /> If you want an even scarier Gorehound with a silver weapon instead of a normal one, a silver hammer is as deadly as a silver machete, and more practical. It's a simple solution to that particular design aesthetic.<br /> <br /> We get it, blades are cool, but silver is not a good blade metal. A classic Gorehound (keeping in mind the second version in W20 that plays into the smarter slashers of movies like Scream instead of a the pure muscle ones) doesn't pick weapons that are cool, they make weapons iconic (and thus cool) because of how deadly they make things that aren't the best weapons: wood axes, kitchen knives, various camp and outdoor equipment, chainsaws, hooks, etc. Michael Myers made a kitchen knife scary, not the other way around.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-24T07:39:39-07:00","id":1465135,"title":"","content":"In the end, few supernaturals can stand indefinitely a good ol'BFG. If you can shot a 12 gauge shotgun enough times before the werewolf reachs you, why care?<br /> <br /> But one thing that occurred to me: anyone else got the impression by the title that it would be about weapons made of silver and Garou body parts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}